.TH MQ_SEND 3 "2026-07-01" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mq_send, mq_timedsend \- send a message to a POSIX message queue
.SH LIBRARY
Realtime library (librt, \-lrt)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <mqueue.h>
.PP
.BI "int mq_send(mqd_t " mqdes ", const char *" msg_ptr ", size_t " msg_len ", unsigned " msg_prio );
.br
.BI "int mq_timedsend(mqd_t " mqdes ", const char *" msg_ptr ", size_t " msg_len ,
.br
.BI "                 unsigned " msg_prio ", const struct timespec *" abs_timeout );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mq_send ()
adds the message pointed to by
.I msg_ptr,
of length
.I msg_len
bytes, to the message queue
.IR mqdes .
The
.I msg_len
must not exceed the queue's
.I mq_msgsize
attribute.
.PP
.I msg_prio
is a non-negative priority less than
.BR MQ_PRIO_MAX .
Messages are queued in decreasing priority order; messages of equal priority
are delivered in the order they were sent (FIFO within a priority).
.PP
If the queue is full and
.B O_NONBLOCK
is not set for the descriptor,
.BR mq_send ()
blocks until space becomes available or the call is interrupted by a signal.
.BR mq_timedsend ()
behaves identically except that if the queue is full it blocks only until the
absolute time
.RB * abs_timeout
(a
.B CLOCK_REALTIME
.BR "struct timespec" ),
after which it fails with
.BR ETIMEDOUT .
A NULL
.I abs_timeout
makes
.BR mq_timedsend ()
block indefinitely, exactly like
.BR mq_send ().
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.  On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
The queue was full and
.B O_NONBLOCK
was set for the descriptor.
.TP
.B EBADF
.I mqdes
is not a valid descriptor open for writing.
.TP
.B EINTR
The call was interrupted by a signal.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I msg_prio
is not less than
.BR MQ_PRIO_MAX ,
or
.RB ( mq_timedsend )
.RB * abs_timeout
is invalid.
.TP
.B EMSGSIZE
.I msg_len
is greater than the queue's
.I mq_msgsize
attribute.
.TP
.B ETIMEDOUT
.RB ( mq_timedsend )
The queue remained full until the timeout expired.
.TP
.B EIDRM
The queue was removed with
.BR mq_unlink (3)
while the call was blocked.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
const char *m = "hello";
if (mq_send(q, m, 6, 3) == \-1)
        perror("mq_send");
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mq_receive (3),
.BR mq_open (3),
.BR mq_getattr (3),
.BR mq_open (2)
